  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 3-10 EUR in the first 10 days of the forecast horizon, failing to anticipate the magnitude of the post-peak crash.",
    "Adjust for momentum lag: The model exhibits a significant lag in reacting to sentiment shifts; when sentiment drops to 0.00 (as seen in Oct 25-30), the model continues to forecast a slow recovery or stability instead of the immediate 10-15% price collapse observed in reality.",
    "Reduce overshoot after volatility spikes: Following price spikes (e.g., the 85.66 peak), the model assumes a gentle mean reversion, whereas the true market behavior is a sharp, accelerated decline that the model fails to capture.",
    "Invert sentiment weighting: High sentiment scores (1.00) in the history often precede price drops in this dataset; the model incorrectly interprets high sentiment as a bullish signal for future price increases, leading to systematic over-forecasting.",
    "Apply horizon-specific decay: For forecasts beyond 15 days, the model's upward drift is structurally flawed; apply a steeper negative slope correction to align with the observed long-term downtrend."
  ]
